It holds Google's three face models and the face at rest they come with:
  face_detector.tflite             - finds faces (BlazeFace, short range)
  face_landmarks_detector.tflite   - Face Mesh V2: 478 points on a face
  face_blendshapes.tflite          - Blendshape V2: 52 face expressions
  geometry_pipeline_metadata_landmarks.binarypb - the face at rest in 3D
Model cards: https://ai.google.dev/edge/mediapipe/solutions/vision/face_landmarker

The file is Google's, unchanged, as downloaded from
https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_landmarker/face_landmarker/float16/1/face_landmarker.task
sha256 64184e229b263107bc2b804c6625db1341ff2bb731874b0bcc2fe6544e0bc9ff

DireBot for OBS runs the models with its own code (src/face/nn); no
MediaPipe or TensorFlow code is part of it.
